DIAGNOSTIC: read the CSI-2 receiver's hardware counters

WHY
---
The whole conclusion of this investigation -"not one symbol reaches the CSID"-
rests on ONE single instrument: the bits of CSI2_RX_IRQ_STATUS. It is validated
with a positive control (the CSID's pattern generator marks SOT and EOT on all
four lanes), but it is still a single instrument.

Qualcomm's CSID register map (cam_ife_csid170.h) declares hardware counters that
mainline NEVER reads:

    0x160   csid_csi2_rx_total_pkts_rcvd    total packets received
    0x168   csid_csi2_rx_total_crc_err      total CRC errors
    0x130   csid_csi2_rx_captured_long_pkt_0
    0x134   csid_csi2_rx_captured_long_pkt_1
    0x3e0   csid_rdi_byte_cntr_ping         bytes counted by RDI0

They are an INDEPENDENT route to the same question:

  packet counter other than zero -> they do arrive, and the fault is further
                                   down; the whole investigation would have
                                   been looking at the wrong place
  counter at zero               -> it confirms it by a second route

And if packets do arrive but with bad CRC, the CRC counter says so and that
points straight at lane order or polarity.

They are read on the stop path, next to the interrupt status that was already
being read there, and are exposed as module parameters so they can be consulted
without depending on the kernel log.

This does NOT fix anything: it is for looking, and above all for not trusting a
single instrument.
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:25:29.785071748 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-gen2.c	2026-08-17 12:25:29.805631597 +0200
@@ -49,6 +49,23 @@
  * interrupciones por fotograma esto puede convertirse en una tormenta, y este
  * movil es sensible a la temporizacion. Se enciende a mano cuando haga falta.
  */
+static unsigned int diag_pkts;
+module_param(diag_pkts, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_pkts, "Paquetes CSI-2 recibidos (contador de hardware, 0x160).");
+
+static unsigned int diag_crc;
+module_param(diag_crc, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_crc, "Paquetes con CRC malo (contador de hardware, 0x168).");
+
+static unsigned int diag_pkt_hdr0;
+module_param(diag_pkt_hdr0, uint, 0644);
+static unsigned int diag_pkt_hdr1;
+module_param(diag_pkt_hdr1, uint, 0644);
+
+static unsigned int diag_bytes_rdi0;
+module_param(diag_bytes_rdi0, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_bytes_rdi0, "Bytes contados por el RDI0 (0x3e0).");
+
 static int cgc_en_reset = 1;
 module_param(cgc_en_reset, int, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(cgc_en_reset,
@@ -422,6 +439,36 @@
 				dev_info(csid->camss->dev,
 					 "csid%d al parar: rx=0x%08x rdin%d=0x%08x\n",
 					 csid->id, rx, i, rdi);
+
+				/*
+				 * LOS CONTADORES DE HARDWARE.
+				 *
+				 * El mapa de registros del CSID de Qualcomm
+				 * (cam_ife_csid170.h) declara contadores que
+				 * mainline no lee NUNCA:
+				 *
+				 *   0x160  total de paquetes recibidos
+				 *   0x168  total de errores de CRC
+				 *   0x130  cabecera del ultimo paquete largo
+				 *   0x134  idem, segunda palabra
+				 *   0x3e0  bytes contados por el RDI0
+				 *
+				 * Son un instrumento INDEPENDIENTE de los bits
+				 * de interrupcion: si el contador de paquetes
+				 * no es cero, es que si llegan y el fallo esta
+				 * mas abajo. Y si es cero, lo confirma por un
+				 * segundo camino.
+				 */
+				diag_pkts = readl_relaxed(csid->base + 0x160);
+				diag_crc = readl_relaxed(csid->base + 0x168);
+				diag_pkt_hdr0 = readl_relaxed(csid->base + 0x130);
+				diag_pkt_hdr1 = readl_relaxed(csid->base + 0x134);
+				diag_bytes_rdi0 = readl_relaxed(csid->base + 0x3e0);
+				dev_info(csid->camss->dev,
+					 "csid%d contadores: paquetes=%u crc_malo=%u cabecera=0x%08x/0x%08x bytes_rdi0=%u\n",
+					 csid->id, diag_pkts, diag_crc,
+					 diag_pkt_hdr0, diag_pkt_hdr1,
+					 diag_bytes_rdi0);
 			}
 
 			__csid_configure_rdi_stream(csid, enable, i);
